        <div class="tab-content" id="tab-updates" data-main="devices" data-sub="updates">
            <div class="info">
                Automatic software updates via <code>winget</code> on Windows devices. Nothing runs automatically until you enable
                it here <strong>and</strong> tick at least one device group; the manual buttons (Run Now, Dry run, per-device and
                per-package actions) work on demand and cover every non-excluded Windows device (a single-device "Update now" also works on an excluded one). Updates are silent, one package at a
                time, and a device is never rebooted. Packages on the ignore list are skipped and (optionally) pinned
                on the client, so even a manual <code>winget upgrade --all</code> leaves license-bound versions
                alone. Devices without winget are reported per run; offline devices are skipped. Automatic runs follow
                a two-stage policy: right after a device connects to the server on a day it has not been updated yet,
                and at the latest 24 h after its previous run - no interval to configure. A full log with one line per
                package is kept below; the Dry run button shows what would happen without touching any machine.
            </div>

            <div class="controls">
                <label><input type="checkbox" id="wgEnabled"> Enable automatic winget updates</label>
                <label><input type="checkbox" id="wgPinSync"> Pin ignored packages on clients</label>

                <button id="wgSaveBtn">Save Configuration</button>
                <button id="wgRunBtn" class="green">Run Now</button>
                <button id="wgDryAllBtn">Dry run all devices</button>
                <span id="wgRunState" class="hint"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="hint">Every change on this tab (switches, groups, ignore list, exclusions, "+ ignore" buttons) is
            saved immediately; the "Save Configuration" button re-applies the whole form explicitly.</div>

            <h3>Device groups to update automatically</h3>
            <div class="table-container"><table>
                <thead><tr><th>Group</th><th style="width:120px;">Auto-update</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody id="wgGroupBody"><tr><td colspan="2" style="color:#888">Loading...</td></tr></tbody>
            </table></div>

            <h3>Ignore list (never auto-upgrade these package ids)</h3>
            <div class="controls">
                <input id="wgIgId" type="text" placeholder="package id, e.g. Adobe.Acrobat.Reader.64-bit" style="min-width:280px;">
                <input id="wgIgNote" type="text" placeholder="reason (optional: license pinned to v11)" style="min-width:240px;">
                <button id="wgIgAdd">Add</button>
            </div>
            <div class="table-container"><table>
                <thead><tr><th style="width:320px;">Package id</th><th>Note</th><th style="width:80px;"></th></tr></thead>
                <tbody id="wgIgBody"></tbody>
            </table></div>
            <div id="wgMsg"></div>

            <h3>Devices</h3>
            <div class="hint">Every Windows device with its winget actions. Excluded machines stay out of all
            automatic batches; "Update now" on a row intentionally still works for them (it targets one device).
            Dry run shows what would happen without touching the machine. After any run, "list" on the row opens
            every package with its outcome (failed ones show the exit code and winget's message), and "+ ignore"
            moves a package onto the ignore list - saved immediately, honoured by every later run.</div>
            <div class="table-container"><table>
                <thead><tr><th style="width:140px;">Device</th><th style="width:110px;">Group</th><th style="width:60px;">Online</th><th style="width:75px;">Excluded</th><th>Last run</th><th style="width:235px;">Actions</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody id="wgDevBody"><tr><td colspan="6" style="color:#888">Loading...</td></tr></tbody>
            </table></div>

            <h3>Packages across all devices (from the stored last runs)</h3>
            <div class="hint">Every winget package your devices reported in their most recent run - aggregate by
            program instead of by machine. "Update everywhere" queues exactly this one package on every
            non-excluded Windows device, "Uninstall everywhere" REMOVES it from every device that has it
            (devices without it are reported as not-installed). "Skipped" counts ignored, version-less and
            not-installed entries. Start a dry run (all) to populate this table.</div>
            <div><button id="wgPkgRefresh" class="small">Refresh package view</button> <span id="wgPkgInfo" class="hint"></span></div>
            <div class="table-container"><table>
                <thead><tr><th style="width:280px;">Package (id)</th><th style="width:190px;">Counts</th><th>Devices (state, versions)</th><th style="width:150px;">Actions</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody id="wgPkgBody"><tr><td colspan="4" style="color:#888">Not loaded yet.</td></tr></tbody>
            </table></div>

            <h3>Update log</h3>
            <div><button id="refreshWgLogBtn" class="small">Refresh log</button> <span id="wgLogInfo" class="hint"></span></div>
            <pre id="wgLog" style="max-height:260px;overflow:auto;background:#0f1720;color:#cfe3f5;padding:8px;border-radius:6px;font-size:11px;margin-top:6px;white-space:pre-wrap;">(not loaded yet)</pre>
        </div>
